MCHL: So your... "escapade" on the moon led you to the Mammoth Project, correct? Why was Shaw so interested in that?

RBTS: Baker figured out pretty quickly that the whole thing was a weapons project. We're not idiots; we all knew what it'd be used for. Who it'd be used against. Why do you think Shaw had so much interest in it?

MCHL: (WITH IMPATIENCE) I need your answer for the record, Lieutenant.

RBTS: He was afraid it'd be used against us, of course. A Soviet super-tank with armour six inches thick and firepower double anything we could come up with? Damn right he was afraid of it. We all were.

MCHL: And was there anything unusual about the project? Anything that suggested it might not have merely been a Soviet superweapon programme?

RBTS: (SARCASTICALLY) It had thicker armour than anything our boys have ever dreamed of and an armament that would put an entire platoon to shame, if that's what you mean - and I'm told it was based on some pretty serious alien tech but that aside, yeah, it seemed pretty normal.

MCHL: (IRRITATED) That's enough, Lieutenant. Now the information that led you to Mars - that was from a series of research notes, yes? What can you tell me about their contents?

RBTS: I never actually saw or handled the notes myself, I'm not technical enough for that sort of thing. That's Baker's department. All I know is that the notes were something to do with the weapons technology the Soviets were developing on the moon. That technology was going to Mars - and that meant we had to follow it.